# Paths under .aiox-core/ that `update-aiox.sh` must NEVER overwrite.
#
# One relative path per line (no leading `.aiox-core/`). A trailing `/` marks a
# directory prefix. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# When upstream ships a different version of a protected file, the update writes
# it alongside as `<file>.upstream-new` instead of overwriting, so the diff can
# be merged by hand.
#
# This file itself does not exist upstream, so it survives every update.

# Project configuration: upstream ships the framework repo's own contributor-mode
# config (frameworkProtection: false, foreign pvMindContext, unused IDEs/MCP).
# Overwriting this silently breaks the project install.
core-config.yaml

# Local fixes to the updater (rsync fallback, protected-path handling).
# Without this line the script would overwrite itself on first run.
scripts/update-aiox.sh
